			"Message": "docs(Grove): Add branded header and polish architecture docs\n\nApply the project-standard dark/light logo banner to the Architecture doc, replacing the plain H1 heading with a branded HTML table header that pairs the Land logo with the Grove title. Update the architecture introduction to use bold formatting on the crate name and align with the 'Architecture' sub-title convention seen across Element docs.\n\nFix the DeepDive opening sentence by removing the superfluous narrative framing ('This document provides the technical foundation for the') and starting directly with the subject ('Grove provides the technical foundation').\n\nBoth documentation pages now follow CodeEditorLand's branded header conventions and present a more direct, scannable opening for readers.",
